{
  "_doc": "Per-agent permissions enforced by scripts/guard.py. Agents not listed here are not restricted by this guard. 'write': glob patterns relative to the project root that the agent may write; 'write_except': globs it may never write ('!pattern' re-includes); 'write_if_conflicted': may edit files that contain merge-conflict markers; 'bash': regexes for SDD commands the agent may run (git, gh, the trace script, \u2026); 'project_commands': purposes from the project's committed .sdd/commands.yaml the agent may run (the registry follows the project's stack; a global denylist always applies; runtime additions via 'deps-add' must be approved in .sdd/dependencies.yaml); chaining and redirection are always denied; 'mcp': 'read-only' denies MCP tools whose name looks like a write. '__hub__' lists the main session's bookkeeping actions that are auto-approved; everything else in the main session keeps normal prompts. In-policy actions are auto-approved unless .sdd/config.yaml sets permissions.auto_approve: false.",
